  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 4907.04 Suspension of Certificate",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 4907.04 Suspension of Certificate.\n\n(a) A certificate shall be suspended if a finding has been made that the certificate holder has:\n\n(1) Given materially false information or made any material misrepresentation in order to obtain a certificate;\n\n(2) Committed misconduct evidenced by:\n\na. Unfitness or incompetence by reason of negligent habits or negligent or willful acts performed in a manner inconsistent with the state and local requirements or applicable codes regulating:\n\n1. Installation of heating equipment systems, domestic water heating systems, or appliances using heating oil; or\n\n2. Servicing and repair of heating equipment, domestic water heating systems, or appliances using heating oils;\n\nb. Unprofessional conduct affecting the practice of the trade;\n\nc. Conduct that negatively affects the health or safety of employees or others; or\n\nd. Willful or repeated violation of the provisions of this chapter, these rules or the state fire code, as adopted in RSA 153:5; or\n\n(3) Not paid any applicable fee under this chapter.\n\nSource. #8650, eff 6-2-06; ss by #9766-A, eff 8-3-10",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c4900.html"
}
